## 10. Compliance & Regulatory

**What it means:** Meeting legal, regulatory, and contractual obligations related to data handling, privacy, and security.

**Key Concepts:**

- **GDPR** — EU data protection regulation. Requires consent, data subject rights (access, deletion), breach notification within 72 hours.

- **CCPA/CPRA** — California privacy laws. Requires disclosure of data collection, opt-out rights, non-discrimination.

- **HIPAA** — US healthcare data protection. Requires safeguards for Protected Health Information (PHI).

- **PCI DSS** — Payment card data security. Required for handling credit card information.

- **SOC 2** — Security audit framework. Type I (point in time) and Type II (over a period).

- **Data Residency** — Requirements about where data must be physically stored.

- **Audit Trail** — Chronological record of system activities for compliance verification.

**What needs to be done:**

- Identify all applicable regulations for your industry and geography
- Classify data by sensitivity level
- Implement consent management where required
- Enable data subject rights (access, export, deletion)
- Set up audit logging for compliance-relevant actions
- Define and enforce data retention policies
- Implement data residency controls if required
- Create privacy policy and terms of service
- Conduct regular compliance audits
- Set up breach notification procedures
- Train team on compliance requirements
- Document all data processing activities
- Implement data anonymization/pseudonymization where needed

**QA Automation:**

- Automate PII detection scanning in databases and logs
- Implement automated consent flow testing
- Create automated tests for data subject rights (access, delete, export requests)
- Automate audit log completeness verification
- Implement automated data retention policy enforcement testing
- Create automated tests for data masking in non-production environments
- Automate compliance report generation
- Implement automated checks for sensitive data in logs
- Create automated tests for breach notification workflows
- Automate data residency verification (ensure data stays in correct region)
- Implement automated encryption verification (at rest and in transit)
- Create automated tests for access control and permission boundaries
- Set up automated compliance drift detection
- Automate testing of cookie consent mechanisms

