## 11. Disaster Recovery & Business Continuity

**What it means:** Preparing for and recovering from catastrophic events that could disrupt system operation.

**Key Concepts:**

- **RTO (Recovery Time Objective)** — Maximum acceptable time to restore service after disaster. "How long can we be down?"

- **RPO (Recovery Point Objective)** — Maximum acceptable data loss measured in time. "How much data can we lose?" If RPO is 1 hour, you need backups at least every hour.

- **Hot Site** — Fully operational duplicate environment, ready to take over immediately.

- **Warm Site** — Partially configured environment that needs some setup time.

- **Cold Site** — Basic infrastructure only, requires significant time to activate.

- **Backup** — Copy of data stored separately for recovery purposes.

- **Replication** — Real-time copying of data to another location.

**What needs to be done:**

- Define RTO and RPO for each critical system
- Identify critical business processes and dependencies
- Implement automated backup strategy
- Set up cross-region data replication for critical data
- Test backup restoration regularly (not just backup creation)
- Create documented disaster recovery plan
- Define roles and responsibilities during disaster
- Set up communication plan for outages
- Conduct DR drills at least annually
- Implement automated failover where possible
- Maintain runbooks for recovery procedures
- Keep contact lists updated
- Plan for various scenarios (region failure, data corruption, ransomware)

**QA Automation:**

- Automate backup creation verification (verify backups are actually created)
- Implement automated backup restoration testing (restore and validate data integrity)
- Create automated failover testing (trigger failover, verify RTO is met)
- Automate RPO verification (measure actual data loss in failure scenarios)
- Implement automated DR drill execution and reporting
- Create automated tests for cross-region replication lag
- Automate runbook execution testing
- Implement automated testing of communication/alerting during DR
- Create automated data corruption detection and recovery tests
- Automate verification of backup encryption
- Implement automated testing of point-in-time recovery
- Create chaos engineering tests for DR scenarios
- Automate verification of backup retention policies
- Set up automated DR environment health checks

