## 13. Data Management

**What it means:** Ensuring data is accurate, consistent, secure, and properly managed throughout its lifecycle.

**Key Concepts:**

- **Data Quality** — Accuracy, completeness, consistency, and timeliness of data.

- **Data Lifecycle** — Stages from creation through archival and deletion. Each stage may have different requirements.

- **Data Retention** — How long data is kept before archival or deletion. Driven by business needs and regulations.

- **Data Governance** — Policies and processes for managing data assets. Includes ownership, stewardship, and standards.

- **Master Data Management** — Ensuring consistent, accurate master data (customers, products) across systems.

- **Data Lineage** — Tracking where data comes from and how it transforms through the system.

**What needs to be done:**

- Define data classification scheme (public, internal, confidential, restricted)
- Assign data owners for each data domain
- Implement data validation at entry points
- Define retention periods for each data type
- Implement automated data archival and deletion
- Set up data quality monitoring
- Create data dictionary documenting all entities
- Implement referential integrity checks
- Plan data migration strategy
- Set up data anonymization for non-production environments
- Document data flows and lineage
- Implement data versioning if needed
- Define data backup and recovery procedures

**QA Automation:**

- Automate data quality checks (accuracy, completeness, consistency)
- Implement automated data validation testing at all entry points
- Create automated tests for data retention policy enforcement
- Automate data archival process verification
- Implement automated referential integrity testing
- Create automated tests for data migration scripts
- Automate data anonymization verification for non-prod environments
- Implement automated schema validation tests
- Create automated tests for data lineage accuracy
- Automate duplicate detection testing
- Implement automated data freshness monitoring
- Create automated tests for data transformation accuracy
- Automate master data consistency checks across systems
- Set up automated data drift detection
- Implement automated testing for data deletion (right to be forgotten)

